                        "sense_id": "bc3df9a6-e4dd-36aa-bdae-de076b3d57b3",
                        "entry_id": "b05e86f1-a8dd-37e8-a7f4-b6c491c2bfc3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A hypothetical base substance from which all chemical elements were believed to have been made; subatomic particles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "historical",
                            "physical",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c40b700d-d7d3-477f-9e9a-4080d42c1a8a",
                                "sense_id": "bc3df9a6-e4dd-36aa-bdae-de076b3d57b3",
                                "text": "Two principles are postulated, according to which the elements have probably been evolved: (1) the ontogenic principle, involving the formation of the primary members of the different groups by direct condensation of protyl; (2) the phytogenetic principle, by which the higher members of the groups are developed from the lower by a process of integration."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94775743-0927-42b8-aa9d-5dbe2585b2f2",
                                "sense_id": "bc3df9a6-e4dd-36aa-bdae-de076b3d57b3",
                                "text": "Dumas wondered whether the fundamental building blocks of atoms might be some smaller division of the hydrogen atom: a half, say, or a quarter. This basic substance became known as ‘protyle’."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
